1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,580
When were you born?
你出生于哪一年？

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:10,730
If it was in the late nineties or early noughties, then you've been classified as being part of Generation Z.
如果是90年代末或21世纪初，那么你将被归类为Z世代的一员。

3
00:00:10,730 --> 00:00:17,610
But what does that mean and is it necessary to group people according to their date of birth?
但这意味着什么，是否有必要根据出生日期对人群进行分组？

4
00:00:17,610 --> 00:00:20,850
People have always been defined by their generation.
人们总是通过世代来定义自己。

5
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:36,865
We had the baby boomers of the 1960s, followed by Generation X and then Generation Y, often referred to as millennials, and the 'new kids on the block' are Generation Z – aged between 16 and 22.
我们有20世纪60年代的婴儿潮一代，接着是X世代，然后是Y世代（通常被称为千禧一代），而“新来的年轻人”是Z世代——年龄在16到22岁之间。

6
00:00:36,865 --> 00:00:45,720
It's easy to classify these young people as being the same, sharing the same attitudes towards life – but is that fair?
很容易将这些年轻人归为一类，并认为他们对生活有相同的态度——但这公平吗？

7
00:00:45,720 --> 00:01:02,840
A survey by the BBC's youth radio channel, Radio One, found that people from Generation Z, informally called 'Z-ers', may be viewed by others as shallow digital natives, incapable of real-world friendships.
BBC青年广播频道Radio One的一项调查发现，Z世代（非正式称为“Z世代人”）可能被他人视为肤浅的数字原住民，无法建立现实世界的友谊。

8
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:11,020
But they actually view themselves as hardworking, entrepreneurial and about to change the world for the better.
但他们实际上认为自己勤奋、有创业精神，并即将让世界变得更好。

9
00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:13,070
It's an ambitious aim.
这是一个雄心勃勃的目标。

10
00:01:13,070 --> 00:01:23,240
The previous generation, born between the mid-1980s and late 1990s - the millennials - were also thought to have these characteristics.
上一代人（出生于20世纪80年代中期至90年代末的千禧一代）也曾被认为具有这些特点。

11
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:31,980
But according to Hiral Patel, an analyst from Barclays, many people view this new generation as "mini-millennials".
但巴克莱分析师希拉尔・帕特尔表示，许多人将这新一代视为“迷你千禧一代”。

12
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:42,710
She told the BBC that Z-ers are different "they have their own set of values and preferences which consumer brands need to cater for.
她告诉BBC，Z世代不同，“他们有自己的价值观和偏好，消费品牌需要迎合这些。

13
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:50,390
Our research found that Gen Z are tech-innate, hyper-informed consumers, and extremely savvy."
我们的研究发现，Z世代是天生懂技术、信息高度灵通的消费者，并且极其精明。”

14
00:01:50,390 --> 00:02:00,940
It's true to say that technology is playing an important part in the lives of Generation Z, particularly in the area of social media.
的确，技术在Z世代的生活中扮演着重要角色，尤其是在社交媒体领域。

15
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:11,550
In fact they have not known life without it and using it to communicate, share ideas and campaign is second nature – it’s their norm.
事实上，他们从未经历过没有技术的生活，使用技术交流、分享想法和发起活动是第二天性——这是他们的常态。

16
00:02:11,550 --> 00:02:18,280
It means they have more of a say on what we eat, drink and buy than any generation before them.
这意味着他们在饮食和购物方面比之前任何一代都更有话语权。

17
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:27,050
These young people certainly need to be listened to by retailers and businesses – they are the people with time on their hands and money.
零售商和企业当然需要倾听这些年轻人的声音——他们有时间也有购买力。

18
00:02:27,050 --> 00:02:30,140
But being a Z-er comes with pressure.
但作为Z世代也伴随着压力。

19
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:37,930
One young person told the BBC survey "many people in Generation Z have mental health issues because they're unsure what the future will bring."
一位年轻人在BBC调查中表示：“许多Z世代有心理健康问题，因为他们不确定未来会带来什么。”

20
00:02:37,930 --> 00:02:48,610
The future always brings uncertainties but maybe there is pressure for this generation to be the most successful ever.
未来总是充满不确定性，但这一代人可能面临着成为最成功一代的压力。

21
00:02:48,610 --> 00:02:52,700
If you're one of them, how do you feel about your future?
如果你是他们中的一员，你对自己的未来有何感受？
